      "description": "Signature unit: state, mono id, title + reason, step · age, one action, aligned columns.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-row\"><span class=\"ds-badge ds-held\"><i></i>held</span><a class=\"ds-id\" href=\"#\">WEB-2006</a><div class=\"ds-title\">Gift-card balance shown for expired cards<small>Two readings of “expired”: which should block checkout?</small></div><span class=\"ds-meta\">triage · 3h</span><button class=\"ds-btn-secondary\">Release…</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:4.5rem 6rem 1fr 7rem 6rem;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:8px 12px;background:var(--color-surface,#12161b);border:1px solid var(--color-border,#2a313a);border-radius:8px;font:400 13px/20px ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--color-fg,#e6e9ef)}.ds-row .ds-id{font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px;color:var(--color-accent,#5b9bff);text-decoration:none}.ds-row .ds-title small{display:block;color:var(--color-muted,#9ba4b4);font-size:12px}.ds-row .ds-meta{color:var(--color-muted,#9ba4b4);font-size:12px;text-align:right}.ds-row .ds-badge{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;border-radius:3px;padding:0 6px;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;color:var(--color-status-held,#e3b341);background:var(--color-status-held-bg,#2e2410)}.ds-row .ds-badge i{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:currentColor}.ds-row .ds-btn-secondary{background:transparent;color:inherit;border:1px solid var(--color-border,#2a313a);border-radius:5px;padding:2px 8px;font:500 12px/16px ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-row .ds-btn-secondary:hover{background:var(--color-surface-raised,#1a2027)}.ds-row .ds-btn-secondary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent,#5b9bff)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Air Traffic Board",
    "overview": "The dashboard is a departures board for agent work. Every ticket is a flight: one row, the same\ncolumns in the same place every time (state, id, title, step and age, the one action), so the eye\nlearns the board once and then only reads what changed. Colour means state and nothing else. A calm\nboard is a dark, even field of quiet rows; when something needs a human, that row is the only thing\non the screen that lights up. It is built to sit on a second monitor and be read in a glance from\nacross the desk.\n\nDensity is high and type is small (13px body), because the operator is technical and the board must\nhold a whole profile without scrolling. Restraint is the default: flat tonal surfaces, hairline\nborders, outline buttons, uppercase section labels in a muted tone. Emphasis is rationed so it keeps\nits meaning.\n\nThe board is meant to feel humane, not clinical. Warmth comes first through words and moments:\nplain-language reasons on every held or failed row, an explicit \"all clear\" when nothing needs you,\na quiet confirmation after an action instead of a row silently vanishing. The current palette is a\ncool slate; a shift toward warm neutrals is the recorded direction (see Colors), not yet the\nimplementation. Dark is primary and light is first-class: both follow the system scheme, and every\ntext and status tier holds WCAG AA in both.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One ticket, one row, columns that line up across every list.",
      "Status hues reserved for state; profile hues reserved for identity.",
      "Flat, tonal, hairline-bordered; shadows only on floating layers.",
      "Monospace for ids, paths, durations, money; sans for everything a person reads.",
      "Small and dense, but never below AA; the faintest tier is furniture, not content.",
      "Warmth through copy and acknowledgement, not decoration."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Colour Is State Rule",
        "body": "A status hue appears only to say a ticket's state. Never decorate with it, never use it on a button, never use it for a profile.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Identity Is Not State Rule",
        "body": "Profile hues mark which profile you are looking at and nothing else. They are held at 3:1 on every surface and kept off the status hues.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Unlit Rule",
        "body": "Faint (#6b7483) is furniture: placeholders, separators, disabled controls. Any text a person needs to read, including timestamps, costs and captions, uses Dim Lamp (muted) or brighter. Faint at 11-12px on content fails AA.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Warm Drift Rule (provisional)",
        "body": "The recorded direction is to move the neutral surfaces from cool slate toward warm neutrals in a future pass, keeping every AA guarantee and the status and identity palettes intact. Until that pass lands, use the tokens as they are; don't hand-tint individual surfaces.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Machine Speaks Mono Rule",
        "body": "Ids, paths, durations, costs and model names are monospace; anything a person wrote or reads as language is sans.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Heading Voice Rule",
        "body": "Zone headings share one style. Don't mix uppercase labels with sentence-case or lowercase headings on the same page.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Board Rule",
        "body": "Nothing on the board itself casts a shadow. If it sits in the page flow, it is separated by tone and hairline, not elevation.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
